[{"id":"VRCE-6-45-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing that Akampana had been killed, the lord of Raksasas, overwhelmed with anger, with his face somewhat fallen, cast his eyes on his counsellors.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"634ab631a6e940c7e958e861a0a4c631423f03376255c7d973bd48d14070190c","compact":"1562dc78aa6c4393a5cb2402828af84b2095edfa7162c1568a0be3ef03f34bda","nasal":"0da38dd8c542f7ddb53460457df2d9e61ad4eaf22b64a8132e9687cd5f4b437a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":2,"english":"Then pondering and reflecting for a while, in the forenoon he went round the city of Lankā for inspecting the barracks.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.907,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"67ae1ff231bdf9befeea7059a38335444a6ddcf4e51523ec97122665d135e527","compact":"8c7c0281c517ca3f7a8372001961afbc36f8c28a20b45801dda757b4dfb5183e","nasal":"67f8ee8755efd0d6dbd7cd9590ff311cb7e324d7449db00a3e2a41810741df2a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":3,"english":"The king surveyed the city guarded by the Rakşsasas, covered with innumerable barracks, and crowned with ensigns and standards,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.794,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"11888921dfa38a8b2cdfe7f27aacfa19379fffb5b29692f7425f50cff3f7ef81","compact":"a3a6c6c0ed9cb4e1883b1c1d27c016269836456aea057a4c4d14d39989fca0a7","nasal":"5b9324ff166fcff32656cacba9eb0cc245bacd0f6825ed8ef643552ccd505ee7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":4,"english":"Seeing the city besieged, Ravana-lord of the Rākşaşas-seasonably spoke words of welfare to Prahasta skilled in fight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.676,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4adaec54d92ef8477aced7a2c6229d8f1c08edc0559036fc1ae3d23a9da2acb0","compact":"8198bc33e0ca73be7eced0953a8685df10c2ed7016d07af47ef7ebae26671212","nasal":"8198bc33e0ca73be7eced0953a8685df10c2ed7016d07af47ef7ebae26671212"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":5,"english":"\"Save battle, deliverance find I none for the city suddenly beleaguered and put to straits.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.785,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"503827e7fb2d7cf8266b78705106b18cc44328a7e6bfa2b646daf53a293f3c31","compact":"a505c5a0e02b9f745986839e109028ea919064f69ba64068f7963d4190a13663","nasal":"a505c5a0e02b9f745986839e109028ea919064f69ba64068f7963d4190a13663"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":6,"english":"And this strain must be borne by these versed in warfare-me or Kumbhakarna or you-my general or Indrajit or Nikumbha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af32a916aaabfe16315f1e6bf2e93ca933d2d495cd114e148418440a3050f4ac","compact":"4b012df448476095d7e627b9b748371af81458f63c656036e6686e7016eed79f","nasal":"21c7a739cc7ccefa9c0abe42d4bde12c6a7f644793b7983e308faeeaa10753f2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":7,"english":"Therefore do you from this place, speedily taking this force, march to where the monkeys are, for securing victory (in the encounter).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.636,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0e2f8baf6e6c971c489beb22cd4dc77c2a73d5c6fca123bc460bdf845ad02f07","compact":"4261537dcd149f77812e6837e1dff546211eef4a9c6e04fb8adb5b5127a5dc03","nasal":"4261537dcd149f77812e6837e1dff546211eef4a9c6e04fb8adb5b5127a5dc03"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":8,"english":"And as soon as you set out, the monkeyforces, hearing the roars of the foremost Rākșasas-speedily setting themselves in motionshall flee away.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.779,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4beb353ac94785f5209f1061934080c1bb5fc411c824a2f9c00c5b6ec7f043df","compact":"f9175cc4911ea81a96d45cd3e3c30c53e09343f5e6d0a29a261bb53c9a412469","nasal":"b0a82157b5f5c320b036b85b33c7b0457acfb51638f8c45766a0cae3a8b4b7b0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":9,"english":"And volatile and haughty and of fickle minds, the monkeys will not be able to bear your shouts; even as elephants are incapable of bearing the roaring of a lion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.817,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cf8f38bd42f638cd64f63d1639eb02dda7af41b5ef00bb987360259c50be81d4","compact":"f252afb23b268c26855e466552a06d4d74e7678500b4a19a6f9b7fa6dd3c01b4","nasal":"4090ffc4f58bc8859e871c0946b76ce69a6a4a6f26d80f5d2854ddba5133ee92"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":10,"english":"And on that monkey-army running away, Rāma in company with Sumitrās son, deprived of his power and shorn of support, shall, O Prahasta, come under your subjection.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.767,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"50be4f46f4213c5d262b0c7ceed7b071cd1c0b7cb4d3a1c976e95897041fcb79","compact":"e0f58802621269bcd40a6563b55a91163d694eb9836433ce12285dc14aaa785c","nasal":"2940cd84851d4651c261db0ff0c0452d64e9fcff80df07bd2353ce12b3c44d1f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":11,"english":"In this matter, your being slain is uncertain, but victory is certain. Now do you, as you weigh out welfare, declare yourself for or against this course.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.823,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e92384188878b881fe1f5ca73cf287677ab96a3723c1658ba842f4f000d6ec43","compact":"6ffbf877c30d729fffe04e2eaa525bff3fff4e59c50d9ac6c80a0e35a6f56ae8","nasal":"6ffbf877c30d729fffe04e2eaa525bff3fff4e59c50d9ac6c80a0e35a6f56ae8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":12,"english":"Thus addressed by Ravana, Prahasta-general of the forces-said to the Rākşaas-chief; like Uśanas addressing the lord of Asuras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2eb3b591a5f1c9544624eed581373ae5ff562b3f4b01a93f2e7780333568e49b","compact":"b588fa12ae24f70c040b50b16cab86209709d87efd63c0a2255273560c3ca8af","nasal":"32ba3054fe1d1ba66b4a9d17cc0670b61f4e1e160553d47169ae668f5e593f55"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":13,"english":"O king before this we had deliberated together with wise counsellors, and then we disputed with each other in our respective views.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0c5cc505fa4a3f20e5f4833439324fd47e0e4b738aebefbe054ccf9f43513aef","compact":"96f82abc5160aca0d1ad6a65222916c047ac06b540e54a5a93dbc17de6f7421d","nasal":"77f969ba3335a3f7838ec01e92e04fd4cc83e7261b266bc5223410832b4428c4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":14,"english":"And I had declared myself for giving up Sītā as fraught with our welfare; and we saw war involved in withholding her.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.71,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"63c72143eec379b943cc9888222f0782144b5553d0dfd1ac0360690650354f81","compact":"82ea65cda60ab111cbb04b3524d2307c4c44a300548ad38b97e24f55b76b6928","nasal":"82ea65cda60ab111cbb04b3524d2307c4c44a300548ad38b97e24f55b76b6928"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":15,"english":"I have ever been honoured by you variously with gifts and regard and soft speech. And what is your good for which I shall not be at the pains?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"11ab8307695efae5c9d42514a36ed1753b593bbb67dc04e82dafb7af27f0a120","compact":"31e7be397c152571d10871c9b8b4e96a2f77e16d028fbac62252393059365ff8","nasal":"da2b284e02e50f7f080323eb7d613645de44d1ce49f726dae3f47dc90765f3b6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":16,"english":"My life I do not care to keep, nor yet my sons or my wife. Behold! for you will I offer up my life into the sacrificial fire of conflict.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b87d2ebfc32329bfe7f71430f9a3f5036763938173fe624a5fad84d0ac2ef6cc","compact":"63c4e05e68783880c18cad6d50b0e3fba74c94c91213a45315f22e6d9c6d3679","nasal":"6d29c05025f43894fcc25b368f7cc3f857bd60788d03c95cfb26305d42523562"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":17,"english":"Having said this to his master-Rävaņa-the general, Prahasta, addressed his generals staying before him, saying. At once bring up the mighty host of Raksasas Today in the field of fight will I entertain the flesh-feeding fowls of the forest with the bodies of the foes slain with my resistless shafts.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.458,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-17","DUTT-6-57-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5ebe563b2f55e08d5ff585cf2f5a6475f82cb7a656e90e0e4553701803363f1c","compact":"76c7d59c