"DUTT-6-57-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2165b808382cb70c44df1273a60d7a1e1cb364d20b3db6b2fcc55a86adca984b","compact":"961dc5aeb2e474e9990f974601bf3ef2d3e01fce2343cc6b983d3fc14dab1b8e","nasal":"c43903113d069baa295d3b79b1c2e0a753ca00b220197ec354a21e65ff476c74"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":21,"english":"In a moment Lankā swarmed with heroic and terrific Rākşasas equipped with various arms, as if with elephants, as well as with people worshipping Fire and bowing down to Brāhmaṇas. And the perfumed breeze blew, laden with the incense of sacrificial offerings.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c2c4622c965bcf507d549ce54403da5ee01e328573867ac9fc24e9f2ce1ae7ef","compact":"3b2e952b09c7f31275bcc9671848b735c2d421972b1a2e09ba8c98aea9e1f8d8","nasal":"eaf2d279aca0ba7345a7331b1d30537d355b42ece3f6a6399dba9c2afb5ae63c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":22,"english":"The Raksasas, inspired with martial ardour, put on diverse garlands, consecrated with scriptural formulae; and donned on their armour.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.845,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aa96bc1910bd3333a6ef526e17cbf677259dc227ab2e06fa4ee454d0b40bdda3","compact":"fb874d2855687e81e1976bf4168fcb03f1cad7ba3f374ce6e11e0769e1f4b873","nasal":"136d071e5f5c86c1ebda37fa360be76a127c3d3b8eacba4ea95c227cc5c68405"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":23,"english":"And furnished with their boys and wearing their armour, the Rākşasas, on seeing king Ravana, leaving (their vehicles), stood, surrounding Prahasta.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"86c542647da0ba0fbc2f4e7f7abd5f5dddf436f2db5c7ad36941366dd8a372a6","compact":"ee91bfce141e79749034a5f7135e4d4ca5aede2a0d8e78381afc5923c11711f6","nasal":"ee91bfce141e79749034a5f7135e4d4ca5aede2a0d8e78381afc5923c11711f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-24","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":24,"english":"The greeting the monarch, Prahasta, furnished (with all appliances of battle), winding his dreadful trumpet, ascended his car; having all sorts of weapons; yoked with wondrous fleet steeds; driven by a competent charioteer, excellently furnished; sending up sounds resembling the rumbling of mighty masses of cloud, appearing like the very sun or Moon; invincible with a serpent-standard; having a defence as well as a portion exceedingly handsome; netted with gold all round; and seeming to be laughing in grace.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.556,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045024","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af470dd9fcc944da1479a948f9dde09967e477f3001fe94dc2ec090ba8dca019","compact":"51f33ecea45d11d00d8bdad3251cfb0352499ec2d95d1fbbc2dceb1aad305d3e","nasal":"9c05342c75d4623de97c7a6fc877b1fcd2a181378e9fcc15ad1a34df06d85826"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-25","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":25,"english":"The greeting the monarch, Prahasta, furnished (with all appliances of battle), winding his dreadful trumpet, ascended his car; having all sorts of weapons; yoked with wondrou