:"Then ascending this car, Prahasta, whom Rāvana had entrusted with authority, surrounded by a vast host, swiftly went out of Larkā. And then there were heard the sounds of kettledrums, resembling the roars of Parjanya, and the sounds of musical instruments, as if filling the Earth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"75a08f3ec93e3aa46fa5d33e00333c776a7fb83cfe4b88ada1c4150573baacbe","compact":"1f3bd84d5b383feac292e56ebdab63b66b0055b7ee8fe4dc8cad4ce45753e81e","nasal":"73ff68480ed2eee70404d0b6efd4cb6f97bce853f1c5c4e57d855a0b01b70e58"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":28,"english":"Then ascending this car, Prahasta, whom Rāvana had entrusted with authority, surrounded by a vast host, swiftly went out of Larkā. And then there were heard the sounds of kettledrums, resembling the roars of Parjanya, and the sounds of musical instruments, as if filling the Earth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.787,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"775755653f4f3a69381d16986da7d1e9ccdc4a98ac2c7bd86b746128050495d4","compact":"85933b7c8e9065c5ceccd5b08a6acfcf4b6191d18b628e8c2a13fba3ad9aab13","nasal":"9935469605aa72fd021cb1b6211b9e88650a46793906423e97d3f9dcae7b52f7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":29,"english":"And on that general of the forces marching, sounds of conchs were heard (all around); and the Rākşasas of dreadful forms and huge bodies, going before Prahasta, advanced, emitting tremendous roars.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.646,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"161d52c8d0c11c39dbabb0d0fc9f4c2a4750fbe4f43329fa60fbd53d6532d543","compact":"66e2a0a9eb80d985c41430ffba83b9c3dc40f13e01fa5d760705720ed3b94b9c","nasal":"0a96ba3f7f16a94c24f2be2b95de75ccce08db60e8f7196893c9daa01a400166"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-30","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":30,"english":"And he went out by the Eastern entrance, environed by this exceedingly dreadful array, resembling troops of elephants.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7a1953425d06418e633ecf3edde98c09ad877e5ce6a02a16aa4bbd9f0a577c5a","compact":"e715921903aea834a021e9350a7d078e55edf341230d17c4f1d7144081f37cc3","nasal":"e715921903aea834a021e9350a7d078e55edf341230d17c4f1d7144081f37cc3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":31,"english":"And resembling the Destroyer-Yama himselfPrahasta in rage went out surrounded by that mighty host resembling the sea.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.597,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84cf1ee58525da9625bc10b506aea5e8b5477db22d2903e99ebfc9a8646067fc","compact":"3e66555efb3406dddc8ff2cffdb348eaf31c40f1a39ac0b3c444751bc112f5f0","nasal":"c9015485ef56aebc42b65ee4a8ba6976652ac293308904595a78ab3293107615"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":32,"english":"And at the tumult raised by their exodus, as well as the roars of the Rākşasas, all creatures in Lankā began to cry in preternatural tones.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045032","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8ddf3e403433e93983c0c0358bb03c633eca8292c97e38fa596a968abcfda7b3","compact":"50f80e747b95c60c9b3fd2af704a6f6175392624496db959a1d142bac0f7fa95","nasal":"174e62f693785c357d865d23be0ee718ac37bca5d5deb85709a864db2e462989"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":33,"english":"And swarming under the cloudless welkin, birds feasting on flesh and gore began to gyrate at the right hand of the car.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cd8feca621a4d9e3eeb3584d8af20acb8d592b401979443848d661bb6bb7f121","compact":"550d3526e7f9176a9356385881a8bfb48f40da59e26c1d5aa0a8ce18758ceb30","nasal":"5cceab710ce3dcc8b74be154f096d15f48520d2485a4238ff19c4ffef5002b60"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-34","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":34,"english":"From the cloudless yet fierce sky meteors began to shoot. and throwing up flames from their mouths, dreadful jackals began to emit cries.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.741,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-53-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"210098697f49163887a63f600da13fa217d4b99121270c33a2502abc63124aae","compact":"fc1f1ee61b29881eb41ee03c306af2f655348b6d5d877157ddcd6f73d6db57c3","nasal":"d612db98ad94bb25456f1ab03af4ac36094c576930fc0d89c0139bf418a87d47"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-35","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":35,"english":"And dreadful jackals, emitting live flames from their mouths, set up cries. And stars began to shoot from the firmament; and the winds to ruffle. And enraged at each other, the planetary bodies were shorn of their brightness. And clouds emitting sharp sounds, showered down blood upon the car, and those marching in front were washed therewith. And alighting at the top of the standard, a vulture set up cries, facing the south and began to prick both its sides, thereby depriving (Prahasta) of his grace.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.429,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-31","DUTT-6-57-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045035","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a2ddfd42d8eb8f54cb5007364e4aa473f074f17a8c4e29d9de414079fa928ff0","compact":"e0e0f1f9f7039c9f3414bd432acfdfb5210beea97b142e3d203efc46884fd673","nasal":"b49401c72a5912af859d13b609e2d679e292b779a97e8a8e83ed99a5bd76d620"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-36","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":36,"english":"And enraged at each other, the planetary bodies were shorn of their brightness. And clouds emitting sharp sounds, showered down blood upon the car, and those marching in front were washed therewith. And alighting at the top of the standard, a vulture set up cries, facing the south and began to prick both its sides, thereby depriving (Prahasta) of his grace.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045036","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"80b00b4186d693ad4ca23d6b17e7e1881554ae3796f4bc83a68f331ae4e299e8","compact":"8310381c8f873e985f353661de67f68f548ed4d8954a07996ec32af50957fd0e","nasal":"8310381c8f873e985f353661de67f68f548ed4d8954a07996ec32af50957fd0e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-37","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":37,"english":"And from the hands of his charioteer and his driver conducting the steeds, never given to turning away from the field the goad began to drop again and again.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.633,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045037","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"16a696ee2f8c87b615267ecb90a49e303c634dc8975630dfda601b38df06bee1","compact":"e14eab94719b5848ebf7162e62323586cb3e5beac671c366b4a6b3af6a83ef8b","nasal":"e14eab94719b5848ebf7162e62323586cb3e5beac671c366b4a6b3af6a83ef8b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-38","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":38,"english":"The auspiciousness that was bright and rare when the army set out, was clean gone in a moment, and the steeds began to stumble on even ground.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045038","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21345425ab3e1893863b6326908bff5fd41efe17ef46a52c94f09f2d0e3e2b41","compact":"028e9f24d87ac13fdfca012d7733ce2d9ada7bce3a49db431ce58194d4ab2af3","nasal":"028e9f24d87ac13fdfca012d7733ce2d9ada7bce3a49db431ce58194d4ab2af3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-45-39","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":45,"verse":39,"english":"And as Prahasta of renowned worth and valour marched, the monkey-army equipped with various arms, presented themselves before him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.698,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-57-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6045039","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ff34596bdd3d67067e9b97bc055536a7d8ddf77e66a0cbd30426bc5c11214eb6","compact":"7a1fd2b1d612bd646ccb49754757300899f18e8b9fbfc52898106ea63b9defb6","nasal":"9cacaf17f2